{"severity":"error","file":"errors/parse_error_9.march","start_line":8,"start_col":11,"end_line":8,"end_col":12,"message":"A `let?` binding can't have a type annotation — its type is inferred from the `Ok` payload of the `Result` on the right.","code":"parse_error","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":8,"start_col":11,"end_line":8,"end_col":17,"text":"","applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":["let? name = result_expr","After this is fixed, `main` will also need permission to print: add `needs IO.Console` to the module, and give `main` the grant, `fn main(_console : Cap(IO.Console))`."],"category":"SYNTAX"}
